  "preregistration_amendments": [
    "backend hqq not optimum-quanto: quanto validates nbits in [2,4], so 8-bit is unreachable and 8/4/2 is not a single-backend curve",
    "q_group_size 32 not the library default 64: group 64 achieves per-channel grouping only for even padded lengths, measured at 38.1% of short batches vs 60.3% of explain batches, which would confound the short-vs-explain contrast",
    "residual_length 512 not the default 128: at 128 a question flushes only if its answer exceeds 128 tokens, making the approximation depend on the outcome",
    "group size added as a second precision axis after the smoke run showed identity saturated at 1.0 for 8- and 4-bit, leaving the 8/4/2 ladder with no resolution between 4 and 2 bits",
    "backend contrast is CPU-proxy only, not EM-level: optimum-quanto 0.2.7 JIT-compiles a monolithic CUDA extension bundling Marlin kernels requiring sm_80; the T4 is sm_75, so the build aborts even though the unpack kernel it needs compiles. No supported way to skip the Ampere-only sources. Environmental, not results-driven. Deliberately NOT deferred to the RTX 4090: different architecture means different kernels, and splitting a mechanism-independence contrast across two GPUs would confound exactly what it isolates. Missed by the P2-5d smoke run, which exercised only hqq \u2014 the backends share one Python entry point but diverge below it, and the audit ran on CPU where quanto never touches the extension."
  ],
  "axis_verified_on_real_kv": "results/knob3_smoke.json",
